{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Waiting for queries to become stale is not always enough. After a mutation succeeds, you often know that related cached data is out of date. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.invalidateQueries"},{"type":"text","value":" to mark matching queries stale and refetch active observers."}]},{"type":"code","value":"queryClient.invalidateQueries()\n\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When a query is invalidated:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is marked stale, overriding any "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"staleTime"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a matching query is active in a controller, it can refetch in the background"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"invalidation-from-mutations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalidation from Mutations"}]},{"type":"code","value":"private readonly addTodo = createMutationController(this, {\n  mutationFn: addTodo,\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n  },\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this pattern when the mutation result tells you related cached data is stale. The "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/pagination","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination example"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows invalidation after project mutations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"query-matching","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Query Matching"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Match a group of queries by prefix:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both of these query keys match:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const projectsListKey = ['projects']\nconst projectsPageKey = ['projects', 1, 250, false]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a more specific key when only one slice should be invalidated:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['projects', this.page],\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"exact: true"},{"type":"text","value":" to match only the exact key:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  exact: true,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"manual-cache-updates","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manual Cache Updates"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalidation is usually simpler than normalized cache updates. When you do need immediate UI updates, combine targeted cache writes with invalidation:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"queryClient.setQueryData<TodosResponse>(['todos'], (existing) => {\n  if (!existing) return existing\n\n  return {\n    ...existing,\n    items: [...existing.items, createdTodo],\n  }\n})\n\nawait queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For rollback with optimistic updates, see the mutation guide and the "},{"type":"link","href":"../examples/pagination","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pagination example"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"invalidation-from-mutations","text":"Invalidation from Mutations","level":2},{"id":"query-matching","text":"Query Matching","level":2},{"id":"manual-cache-updates","text":"Manual Cache Updates","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nWaiting for queries to become stale is not always enough. After a mutation succeeds, you often know that related cached data is out of date. Use `queryClient.invalidateQueries` to mark matching queries stale and refetch active observers.\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries()\n\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n})\n```\n\nWhen a query is invalidated:\n\n- It is marked stale, overriding any `staleTime`\n- If a matching query is active in a controller, it can refetch in the background\n\n## Invalidation from Mutations\n\n```ts\nprivate readonly addTodo = createMutationController(this, {\n  mutationFn: addTodo,\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUse this pattern when the mutation result tells you related cached data is stale. The [Pagination example](../examples/pagination) shows invalidation after project mutations.\n\n## Query Matching\n\nMatch a group of queries by prefix:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] })\n```\n\nBoth of these query keys match:\n\n```ts\nconst projectsListKey = ['projects']\nconst projectsPageKey = ['projects', 1, 250, false]\n```\n\nUse a more specific key when only one slice should be invalidated:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['projects', this.page],\n})\n```\n\nUse `exact: true` to match only the exact key:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  exact: true,\n})\n```\n\n## Manual Cache Updates\n\nInvalidation is usually simpler than normalized cache updates. When you do need immediate UI updates, combine targeted cache writes with invalidation:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.setQueryData<TodosResponse>(['todos'], (existing) => {\n  if (!existing) return existing\n\n  return {\n    ...existing,\n    items: [...existing.items, createdTodo],\n  }\n})\n\nawait queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n```\n\nFor rollback with optimistic updates, see the mutation guide and the [Pagination example](../examples/pagination).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: query-invalidation\ntitle: Query Invalidation\n---\n\nWaiting for queries to become stale is not always enough. After a mutation succeeds, you often know that related cached data is out of date. Use `queryClient.invalidateQueries` to mark matching queries stale and refetch active observers.\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries()\n\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['todos'],\n})\n```\n\nWhen a query is invalidated:\n\n- It is marked stale, overriding any `staleTime`\n- If a matching query is active in a controller, it can refetch in the background\n\n## Invalidation from Mutations\n\n```ts\nprivate readonly addTodo = createMutationController(this, {\n  mutationFn: addTodo,\n  onSuccess: async () => {\n    await queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n  },\n})\n```\n\nUse this pattern when the mutation result tells you related cached data is stale. The [Pagination example](../examples/pagination) shows invalidation after project mutations.\n\n## Query Matching\n\nMatch a group of queries by prefix:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['projects'] })\n```\n\nBoth of these query keys match:\n\n```ts\nconst projectsListKey = ['projects']\nconst projectsPageKey = ['projects', 1, 250, false]\n```\n\nUse a more specific key when only one slice should be invalidated:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['projects', this.page],\n})\n```\n\nUse `exact: true` to match only the exact key:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.invalidateQueries({\n  queryKey: ['projects'],\n  exact: true,\n})\n```\n\n## Manual Cache Updates\n\nInvalidation is usually simpler than normalized cache updates. When you do need immediate UI updates, combine targeted cache writes with invalidation:\n\n```ts\nqueryClient.setQueryData<TodosResponse>(['todos'], (existing) => {\n  if (!existing) return existing\n\n  return {\n    ...existing,\n    items: [...existing.items, createdTodo],\n  }\n})\n\nawait queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['todos'] })\n```\n\nFor rollback with optimistic updates, see the mutation guide and the [Pagination example](../examples/pagination).\n"}
